= AI agent — Technical =

== System formulation ==
A modern AI-agent system can be modeled as a policy over internal state, observations, goals, available actions/tools, and execution history:

<pre>
a_t ~ π(a | o_≤t, s_t, g, T_t)
</pre>

with environment/tool response producing new observations and state.

The policy may be implemented by an LLM, reinforcement-learning policy, planner, symbolic controller, or compound architecture.

== Compound system ==
Typical architecture can include:

<pre>
model
+ orchestration/controller
+ tool/action interfaces
+ memory/state
+ retrieval
+ monitor/evaluator
+ permission boundary
</pre>

Agent behavior therefore depends on the compound system, not only model weights.

== Taxonomy caution ==
Current literature uses “AI agent”, “LLM agent”, “autonomous agent”, and “agentic AI” inconsistently.

Technical claims should specify architecture and degree of autonomy rather than infer properties from the label alone.

